flowchart TB
    accTitle: The newest documents on the dashboard
    accDescr: The dashboard of jamie asks the widget New in Paperless for its items. The app takes a page of the 25 documents that Paperless-ngx added last from Nextcloud's distributed cache, or else asks Paperless for it, newest first, and keeps it for a minute for every user, since every request carries the token of the settings. Of these, jamie sees the documents whose file jamie can open, found by their markers in one search of the file cache. While fewer than seven are found and Paperless has older documents, the app takes the next page the same way, up to four pages, the 100 newest documents, and then, where Paperless Sync gives each owner an archive, the 25 newest documents of jamie's own user of Paperless. jamie sees at most seven, with the names of their correspondents, types and tags. Each item shows the preview of its file, its title, and the day that Paperless added it, its correspondent, its type and up to two of its tags, such as Sep 3, 2026 · Example Motors · Receipt · warranty, and opens the file in Files.

    dashboard["The dashboard of jamie asks<br>New in Paperless for its items"]
    cache{"The newest documents<br>in the cache of Nextcloud?"}
    paperless[("Paperless-ngx: a page of the 25 documents<br>added last, newest first,<br>at most once a minute for every user")]
    files["The files that jamie can open,<br>by their markers,<br>in one search of the file cache"]
    more{"Fewer than seven, and<br>Paperless has older documents?"}
    names["The names of their correspondents, types and tags,<br>kept for ten minutes"]
    widget(["`**The newest documents of jamie**, at most seven:
    the preview of the file, the title,
    Sep 3, 2026 · Example Motors · Receipt
    *each opens its file in Files*`"])

    dashboard --> cache
    cache -- "no" --> paperless
    paperless --> files
    cache -- "yes" --> files
    files --> more
    more -- "yes: the next page, up to four,<br>then the newest of jamie's own owner" --> cache
    more -- "no" --> names
    names --> widget

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef app fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef yes fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class dashboard you
    class cache,files,more,names app
    class widget yes
